{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/main/schema/mbmap-2.schema.json",
  "mbmap": 2,
  "vendor": "Mercato Automação",
  "model": "MEP",
  "vendor_website": "mercatoautomacao.com.br",
  "description": "Pressurized stairwell controller (Climate line) with two fan outputs, PID pressure control, smoke detector and damper inputs; Modbus RTU or BACnet MS/TP on RS485",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-18",
  "firmware": "Modbus table version 0",
  "source": "Mercato Automação, Climate MEP user manual, revision A (2020-11-17)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Climate MEP - Manual do usuário",
      "version": "Revision A",
      "date": "2020-11-17",
      "url": "https://mercatoautomacao.com.br/documentacoes/produtos/Climate/MEP/Manual%20do%20Integrador/MEP%20-%20Manual%20do%20usu%C3%A1rio.pdf",
      "note": "section 7, Modbus table",
      "accessed": "2026-11-18",
      "sha256": "c0c7f5d09d6257267356fa4ceb04b6a29ec39c54a52e8c1a1bb472a180ee77a0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU slave on the isolated RS485 port (up to 115200 bit/s); the port protocol (Modbus or BACnet MS/TP), speed, parity, stop bits and address are set in the Comunic group of the setup menu. The manual gives no factory values. Functions 03, 04, 06, 16 and 43; 03 and 04 read the same registers.",
    "FLOAT and 32-bit values take two registers, most significant first. Each FLOAT register can also be read as a 16-bit integer, multiplied by 10, at the address plus 20000 (for example the pressure at 20000).",
    "The setup values (pressures, PID, fan rotation, communication) are only set on the local keypad and are not in the Modbus table.",
    "The manual does not say which values the status inputs return besides zero and non-zero; the on/off table assumes 1 is active.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "databits": 8,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
  "enums": {
    "on_off": {"0": "Off", "1": "On"}
  },
